  READ THIS AS: I3 is the identity the lossless argument does NOT need, I2 is the one
  that legitimately leaves a quadratic form, and I1 is the one whose boundary term the
  draft mis-stated. The ANTISYM row is the control: it must be LARGE, because only the
  symmetric part of H is annihilated. If it were small, the test would be vacuous.

==========================================================================================
SUMMARY
==========================================================================================
  A identities symbolically      : PASS
  B nine cells reduced           : see the table; TWO cells had the wrong boundary
    condition in the draft (I1, positions return, not velocities vanish)
  C identities on the real data  : see the residual columns above
  The lossless obstruction (dissipative vs damping) needs NO boundary condition and
  is unaffected by the correction.
